 "title": {
  "en": "Ampère's circuital law and the solenoid",
  "kn": "ಆಂಪಿಯರ್‌ನ ಆವರ್ತ ನಿಯಮ ಮತ್ತು ಸೊಲೆನಾಯ್ಡ್"
 },
 "minutes": 40,
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "Walk once around the current",
    "kn": "ಪ್ರವಾಹದ ಸುತ್ತ ಒಂದು ಸುತ್ತು"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "Gauss's law made symmetric electric problems easy. Ampère's circuital law does the same for magnetism: walk once round a closed loop, and the field along it tells you the current inside.",
    "kn": "ಗಾಸ್ ನಿಯಮ ಸಮಮಿತ ವಿದ್ಯುತ್ ಸಮಸ್ಯೆಗಳನ್ನು ಸುಲಭಗೊಳಿಸಿತು. ಆಂಪಿಯರ್‌ನ ಆವರ್ತ ನಿಯಮ ಕಾಂತತ್ವಕ್ಕೆ ಅದೇ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "State Ampère's circuital law and use it for a long straight wire."
    },
    {
     "en": "Find the field inside a long solenoid."
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Gauss's law made symmetric electric problems easy. Ampère's circuital law does the same for magnetism: walk once round a closed loop, and the field along it tells you the current inside.",
    "kn": "ಗಾಸ್ ನಿಯಮ ಸಮಮಿತ ವಿದ್ಯುತ್ ಸಮಸ್ಯೆಗಳನ್ನು ಸುಲಭಗೊಳಿಸಿತು. ಆಂಪಿಯರ್‌ನ ಆವರ್ತ ನಿಯಮ ಕಾಂತತ್ವಕ್ಕೆ ಅದೇ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Ampère's circuital law"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The line integral of B around any closed loop equals μ₀ times the current threading the loop: $\\oint\\vec B\\cdot d\\vec l = \\mu_0 I_{enc}$. For a long straight wire, take a circle of radius r: $B\\cdot2\\pi r = \\mu_0I$, so $B = \\mu_0I/2\\pi r$. The field lines are concentric circles around the wire; the right-hand thumb rule gives their sense.",
    "kn": "ಆಂಪಿಯರ್ ನಿಯಮ: ∮B·dl = μ₀I_ಒಳಗೆ. ಉದ್ದ ನೇರ ತಂತಿಗೆ B = μ₀I/2πr; ಕ್ಷೇತ್ರ ರೇಖೆಗಳು ತಂತಿಯ ಸುತ್ತ ಏಕಕೇಂದ್ರೀಯ ವೃತ್ತಗಳು."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "∮B · dl = μ₀I_enc"
    },
    {
     "en": "Long wire: B = μ₀I/2πr"
    },
    {
     "en": "Field lines: concentric circles"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Ampère's law says the sum of B along a closed loop equals mu nought times the current inside. For a long straight wire this gives B equals mu nought I by 2 pi r, in circles around the wire.",
    "kn": "ಆಂಪಿಯರ್ ನಿಯಮ: ∮B·dl = μ₀I_ಒಳಗೆ. ಉದ್ದ ನೇರ ತಂತಿಗೆ B = μ₀I/2πr; ಕ್ಷೇತ್ರ ರೇಖೆಗಳು ತಂತಿಯ ಸುತ್ತ ಏಕಕೇಂದ್ರೀಯ ವೃತ್ತಗಳು."
   },
   "formula": "\\oint \\vec B\\cdot d\\vec l = \\mu_0 I_{enc},\\qquad B_{wire} = \\frac{\\mu_0 I}{2\\pi r}"
  },
  {
   "id": "wb1",
   "type": "whiteboard",
   "title": {
    "en": "On the board: Ampère's law: wire and solenoid"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Round a long straight wire the field lines are circles, and B is the same all round a circle of radius r. Take one circle as the Amperian loop: B × 2πr = μ₀I, so B = μ₀I/2πr. Example: 5 A at 4 cm from the wire gives B = 2 × 10⁻⁷ × 5 / 0.04 = 2.5 × 10⁻⁵ T. In a long solenoid the field inside is uniform and along the axis; outside it is nearly zero. Ampère's law on the rectangle gives B L = μ₀ n L I, so B = μ₀ n I. Example: 500 turns on 0.5 m carrying 5 A: n = 1000 per metre, so B ≈ 6.3 × 10⁻³ T."
   },
